<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 3.347 off UK's FTSE 100 index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 3.347 off UK's FTSE 100 index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 index stocks will go ex-dividend on Monday and the the effect will be to take 3.347 points off the index.</p>
<p>						    DIVIDEND    INDEX</p>
<p>						    (PENCE)     EFFECT</p>
<p>		  COMPANY			Net   Gross  Gross</p>
<p>* Bank of Scotland			   2.91   3.64   0.253</p>
<p>* British Gas				  6.40   8.00   2.062</p>
<p>* Great Universal Stores		  11.50  14.38   0.846</p>
<p>* Smith &amp; Nephew			     2.29   2.86   0.185</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
